        },
        {
          "id": "claims",
          "label": "Claims",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 15
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Twilite Has a 3D Host Slot and Nothing In It",
        "definition": "`VIEW_HOSTS = ['web', '3d', 'vr', 'ar', 'map', 'native']` in `components/GraphEditor/utils/surfaceChains.js`. A View's payload can already name a `3d` host so a Surface chain can offer a 3D representation, but nothing in the app renders one; only the web host is implemented.",
        "documentation": "This is why the question is live at all: Twilite's Surface/View model was already built to let a chain end in something other than a web page. A 3D host would slot in the same place a web View does today, once something exists to hand it to.",
        "examples": "",
        "notes": "Verified by reading surfaceChains.js directly on 2026-09-25.",
        "definitionKey": "topic-concept",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "topic-concept",
          "sourceRef": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/topic-template/classes/nodes/topic-concept.node-class.node"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "opensim-3d-host-candidate"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "osim-c-map",
      "type": "topic-concept",
      "label": "Concept",
      "position": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": 220
      },
      "width": 460,
      "height": 320,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
