          "angle": 15
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "A Proposed Twilite-to-OpenSim Mapping",
        "definition": "The design conversation sketched a rough correspondence, offered as a shape, not a spec: `Node → SceneObject`, `Edge → relationship/link/constraint`, `Property → object property`, `Method → behavior/script action`, `Event → simulator event`, `Detail → region/environment experience`.",
        "documentation": "Not all of these are one-to-one. A Twilite Bridge, Portal or Field has no obvious OpenSim counterpart in the sketch, and OpenSim's permission/ownership model is richer than anything Twilite's authority contract currently states. Treat the table as a starting hypothesis for the adapter in gm-mech, not as an agreed contract.",
        "examples": "A Twilite `content` node holding a description could become a `SceneObjectPart`'s description field; a Twilite `method` with declared effects could become an OpenSim LSL-equivalent script action, if OpenSim's scripting sandbox allows an external call in.",
        "notes": "",
        "definitionKey": "topic-concept",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "topic-concept",
