      "data": {
        "title": "Design conversation: \"SceneGraph.cs\"",
        "citation": "Pasted excerpt from a ChatGPT design conversation, shared 2026-09-25; the surrounding conversation was not available to read.",
        "contribution": "The claim that OpenSim already has a class named `SceneGraph`, the `SceneObjectGroup`/`SceneObjectPart`/root-part/linkset sketch, and the proposed Node/Edge/Property/Method/Event/Detail mapping all come from this excerpt, not from reading the OpenSim source directly.",
        "provenance": "Secondary and informal: one participant's paraphrase of the OpenSim source and a linked GitHub repository (`github.com/opensim/opensim`), not the repository itself. Only this one fragment of the conversation was pasted; earlier turns it refers to (\"your antenna went up\") were not seen.",
        "documentation": "Re-read the actual opensim/opensim repository before relying on any specific claim here — see the open questions.",
